core identity of this folder:

    grounded in:
        scripture "Let all things be done decently and in order"
            from 1 Corinthians 14:40 in KJV
        principle "Configuration defines behavior — settings shape operation"
        anchor "Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established"
            from Proverbs 16:3 in KJV

    serves as Settings:
        role "Runtime configuration for state machine operation"
        paradigm "Configuration-driven behavior"

    authored by:
        architect "Seanje Lenox-Wise"
        implementation "Nova Dawn (CPI-SI)"
        created 2025-12-10
        version a-01.00
        modified 2026-01-01 for "Initial root.omni creation"

    exists to:
        purpose "Store runtime configuration by category"
        design "By-concern — display, feedback, monitoring, safety, session, validation"
        philosophy "Configuration as code — settings are explicit and version-controlled"
        features:
            "Display — output formatting and presentation"
            "Feedback — build feedback patterns"
            "Monitoring — log analysis patterns"
            "Safety — critical paths and dangerous patterns"
            "Session — initialization and reminders"
            "Validation — formatters and validators"

interface of this folder:

    depends on:
        requires (1) "bereshit/tov/data/system/" for "containment in system"
        includes (0) "claude-global/hooks/lib/" for "config consumption"
        excludes (-1) "runtime data" because "configuration only"
        used by "Hooks, validators, formatters"
        integrates with "Go packages reading config"

    integrated as:
        navigation "cd bereshit/tov/data/system/config/" for "entering configuration"
        navigation "ls -la" for "viewing config categories"
        exits tov (0) for "configuration found"

operational context of this folder:

    blocking:
        no (-1) because "configuration is read-only at runtime"
        mitigation "validate config on load"

    health:
        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "configuration valid and complete"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "configuration needs attention"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "configuration broken"

        operations:
            "config parses" scores +25 (1) for "all config files valid"
            "categories complete" scores +15 (1) for "all categories present"
            "parse error" scores -30 (-1) for "config file invalid"

        cascade multipliers:
            "runtime dependency" multiplies by 1.8 because "config affects all operations"

